course: dictionary
lesson: 5722
title: Loose: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word loose has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one is meant. Read the words around it and ask: what does loose mean here? «When you get off, you make sure bag straps, drawstrings and loose clothes do not catch on the handrail or door.» Loose clothes are clothes that are not tight, so they can catch on things.
explain: «Loose garden netting can trap birds and hedgehogs, so it is kept tight or taken away.» The word tight is a clue: loose is the opposite. Loose netting is not fixed firmly, so it is dangerous. Try your meaning in the sentence: loose netting can trap birds. That makes sense.
explain: In maths, loose means not packed into a group. «3 bags of 10 marbles and 4 loose marbles are 30 + 4 = 34 marbles.» The 4 loose marbles are not in bags, so you add them on separately.
explain: «A helmet fits snug and level, just above the eyebrows, with the strap buckled; a loose helmet does not protect.» Snug is the clue: a snug helmet fits tightly, so a loose helmet does not fit tightly. A helmet that moves about cannot protect your head.
fact: Loose means not tight, like loose clothes or a loose belt.
fact: Loose means not fixed firmly, like a loose tooth or a loose screw.
fact: Loose means not packed in a box or bag, like loose pencils or loose change.
fact: Loose can also mean free, not tied up or shut in: the dog got loose.
fact: Loosen is the verb: to make something less tight, such as loosening a knot.
exercise: «When you get off, you make sure bag straps, drawstrings and loose clothes do not catch on the handrail or door.» What does loose mean in loose clothes? | Very wet | Dirty | Lost | *Not tight
exercise: «3 bags of 10 marbles and 4 loose marbles are 30 + 4 = 34 marbles.» In this sum, what does loose mean? | Lost forever | Very small | Tied together | *Not packed in a bag
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Loose garden netting can trap birds and hedgehogs, so it is kept tight or taken away.» that means the opposite of loose. | hedgehogs | *tight | birds | netting
test: Mia's tooth wobbles when she touches it. What does loose mean in loose tooth? | Very sore | Growing back | *Not fixed firmly | Painted white
test: The dog got loose in the park. What does loose mean here? | Asleep under a tree | Very tired | Covered in mud | *Free, not tied up or shut in
exam: In «a loose helmet does not protect», what does loose mean? | Very heavy | Brand new | Painted red | *Not fitting tightly, so it can move about
